"type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "whimsical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fanciful; unconventional", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Great Gatsby is such a whimsical movie!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about the 1920's.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swanky", "type": "name"}, {"content": "stylishly luxurious and expensive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The women of the 1920's were swanky.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fancy; fashionable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The women's dresses were swish.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to swoon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to faint from extreme emotion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I swoon every time I think of the fashion back then.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "corset", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a tight undergarment worn to shape a woman's body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women celebrated being free of the corset.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be empowered", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give someone power to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women were empowered by the right to vote.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swashbuckling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "adventurous", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Gatsby was a swashbuckling character.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Stressing New Information", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to stress new information, you use different intonation and stress on the \u201cnew\u201d word or idea.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You generally stress content words in a sentence.<br/> Content words refer to nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs, etc, which are the words that contain the most meaning. <br/>Other words are function words. Function words refer to prepositions, pronouns, auxiliary verbs, conjunctions (like <span class=\"italic\">and</span> and <span class=\"italic\">but</span>). <br><br/>When you want to introduce new information in a conversation, you can choose to put the stress and the intonation on the \u201cnew\u201d words. This helps the listener understand that you want to stress that word and that it is important.  <br><br>Look at this simple conversation:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: I <span class=\"strong\">need</span> a <span class=\"strong\">pair</span> of <span class=\"strong\">shoes</span>. <br><span class=\"strong\">Jason</span>: What <span class=\"strong\">kind</span> of shoes? (\u201ckind\u201d is the new information, \u201cshoes\u201d is the old) <br><span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: <span class=\"strong\">Dress</span>  shoes. <br><span class=\"strong\">Jason</span>: Any <span class=\"strong\">color </span>of dress shoes? <br><span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: <span class=\"strong\">Black</span> dress shoes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you stress these \u201cnew\u201d words, the pitch of your voice will rise and your voice will be louder. This makes the word stand out more in the sentence. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Linking and Deletion With Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to express the highest  of a quality. You use a superlative adjective to talk about one thing or person in a group of things. You always use <span class=\"italic\">the</span> with the superlative.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In natural conversation, it is common to link and delete some sounds in the superlative adjective if there is a similar sound in the next word. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br>The strangest story.  <br>You delete the \u2018t' sound and link the \u2018s' sound. <br>The stranges_story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes this makes it hard to listen to native speakers talk. If you know the rule, you can listen better. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading these words aloud: <br> The smallest sweater  =  The smalles_sweater <br>The loudest truck = The loudes_truck", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "What are your top 3 movies?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What do you like about them?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the things that you like the most about the movies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe them using superlative adjectives.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I think of my top 3 movies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss them with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I like best in the movies.", "type": "text"}]}]}